# Process 10, the body of main.signIn: with an issuer, it builds the sign-in
# middleware around the reloader from the sign-in configuration of box 12;
# without one, it returns the reloader unchanged. Box 10.2 is the
# middleware's answer to each request that the HTTP server sends it:
# signin.New does not call it, as portal.New does not call box 3.4 in
# flow.3.dfd.
# By hand: dfd --box 300x150 --per-row 5 --number --number-prefix 10. docs/flow.10.dfd -o flow.10.svg

{12 Make the sign-in configuration}
> sign-in configuration, reloader
[10.1. Build the sign-in middleware around the reloader: check the sign-in configuration, and discover an OpenID Connect provider's endpoints at its issuer
 or refuse a configuration that cannot sign in a reader
 (signin.New)]
    > issuer
    < provider metadata
    <Identity provider>
    < endpoint
    <Provider>
> sign-in middleware
{HTTP server}
> response writer, request
[10.2. Answer each request: end the session at the sign-out path, finish a sign-in at the callback, serve a signed-in reader's request with the reader's identity, and start a sign-in for any other request
 (signin.middleware.ServeHTTP)]

# type: sign-in configuration = signin.Config
# type: reloader = net/http.Handler
# type: issuer = string
# type: provider metadata = []byte
# type: endpoint = golang.org/x/oauth2.Endpoint
# type: sign-in middleware = net/http.Handler
# type: response writer = net/http.ResponseWriter
# type: request = *net/http.Request
